 ## Overview
-Neural Volume Scattering Prediction is a method for rendering participating media that uses a neural network to predict the scattering distribution at the centers of sampling templates, which is then used to solve the radiative transfer equation [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its sibling [Neural Radiative Transfer Equation Solver](8466-neural-radiative-transfer-equation-solver.md) and the earlier [Radiance-Predicting Neural Networks (RPNN)](7049-radiance-predicting-neural-networks-rpnn.md) by decomposing input features into density, transmission, and phase, and by using specific sampling templates (diffuse and highlight) to simplify the network structure and input parameters, thereby addressing RPNN's inability to handle shadows and its requirement for large sampling [S1, unofficial].
